<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for a ``Lazy to Text.app`` signed with a real Apple
    Developer ID — the only shape Apple will notarize.

    One key, and the reason this file exists is the hardened runtime
    rather than any capability of its own. Apple requires the runtime
    for notarization — "To upload a macOS app to be notarized, you must
    enable the Hardened Runtime capability" — and the runtime denies the
    microphone unless ``com.apple.security.device.audio-input`` is
    declared. A dictation app that opens no microphone is not a
    dictation app, so this is the minimum that makes the build both
    notarizable and functional.

    What is deliberately absent, each because the app does not do the
    thing it would authorise:

    ``com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation``
        Every nested library and Python extension carries the same
        Team ID as the bundle, so validation passes on its own and this
        key would turn off a real protection against a tampered dylib
        for nothing. It is needed for the *self-signed* build — see
        scripts/entitlements-local.plist for why, and for the measured
        failure without it.

    ``com.apple.security.automation.apple-events``
        The autopaste posts keystrokes through Quartz ``CGEventPost``
        (app/clipboard_manager.py), not through AppleScript, so nothing
        here sends Apple events.

    ``com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit`` / ``allow-unsigned-executable-memory``
        Python does not JIT. ONNX Runtime's CoreML provider hands Metal
        shaders to the system compiler, which is not executable memory
        this process supplies.

    Accessibility and Microphone *permissions* are not entitlements —
    they are TCC grants the user makes, keyed to the bundle's designated
    requirement (see scripts/setup-signing.sh). No entry here grants or
    bypasses either.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>